# Files Cloudflare Pages must NOT upload.
#
# The Pages project builds from the repository root (wrangler.toml sets
# pages_build_output_dir = "."), and the root is ~958 MB: the social-media build
# workspace alone carries 376 MB of fonts and cut-outs, and
# social-media/models/EDSR_x2.pb is 38 MB - past Cloudflare's 25 MiB per-file
# asset limit. That single file is why every Cloudflare-side build failed with
# "No deployment available" while the GitHub Actions workflow (which staged a
# small .pages-dist folder) kept succeeding beside it.
#
# With the excludes below the deployment is 128 files / 93 MB, largest file
# 3.2 MB - the same set the Actions workflow has always shipped:
#   index.html app.js style.css logo.svg wrangler.toml data/ functions/ images/
#
# Syntax is .gitignore's. Keep this in step with the "Prepare Pages artifact"
# step in .github/workflows/deploy-cloudflare-pages.yml.

# The build workspace: renderers, fonts, Nuno cut-outs, campaign outputs, models.
social-media/

# Featured-jobs automation - runs in CI, never served.
automation/

# Repo tooling and docs.
.github/
.claude/
.wrangler/
scripts/
*.md
